  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Nucleophilicity of sulfur-containing nucleophiles (such as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>SH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>) is higher than that of oxygen-containing nucleophiles (such as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>).&nbsp; Here Sulphur containing nucleophile can donate its lone pair. A stable carbocation is formed next, stable carbocation will be that which is away from CN group.&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/41a12575-000f-4900-84dd-c553fdaab37f.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 116px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
